1
00:00:02,199 --> 00:00:05,105
So as you saw at this example with the

2
00:00:05,394 --> 00:00:06,758
hx-redirect header,

3
00:00:07,401 --> 00:00:10,499
it can sometimes make sense to set special

4
00:00:10,612 --> 00:00:13,822
headers on the responses in order to change

5
00:00:13,919 --> 00:00:16,632
the client-side behavior of HTMX.

6
00:00:17,997 --> 00:00:20,068
Of course, that also implies that you need

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,877
to own the backend code though. If you can't

8
00:00:22,893 --> 00:00:24,900
make changes to that code, you of course

9
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:26,409
can't set headers like this.

10
00:00:27,725 --> 00:00:30,116
That being said, that's not the only kind of

11
00:00:30,116 --> 00:00:31,368
header you can set though.

12
00:00:32,604 --> 00:00:34,947
Instead, you can, for example, also set

13
00:00:35,107 --> 00:00:38,381
these headers here, Reswap, Retarget, and

14
00:00:38,558 --> 00:00:39,328
Reselect

15
00:00:39,906 --> 00:00:44,592
to change how HTMX will swap the returned

16
00:00:44,656 --> 00:00:47,400
response content into the rendered DOM

17
00:00:48,411 --> 00:00:51,958
or to change which element will be targeted

18
00:00:52,038 --> 00:00:54,574
by HTMX. So that you can essentially

19
00:00:54,911 --> 00:00:58,024
override the settings that were set with

20
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,885
those HTMX attributes

21
00:01:00,447 --> 00:01:01,538
with these headers here.

22
00:01:03,014 --> 00:01:04,955
And I'll show you an example for that.

23
00:01:05,934 --> 00:01:09,480
Here in the POST login route, we're

24
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,780
validating the user input.

25
00:01:12,176 --> 00:01:14,439
And if there is an error in the input, we're

26
00:01:14,503 --> 00:01:17,423
sending back a response where we return this

27
00:01:17,632 --> 00:01:20,119
unordered list with the error messages that

28
00:01:20,119 --> 00:01:20,745
we collected.

29
00:01:22,164 --> 00:01:24,635
Now, if that would be a real application

30
00:01:24,652 --> 00:01:25,055
here though,

31
00:01:25,782 --> 00:01:28,787
validation errors would not be the only kind

32
00:01:28,787 --> 00:01:31,173
of errors that could occur when a user is

33
00:01:31,269 --> 00:01:31,800
logged in.

34
00:01:33,359 --> 00:01:35,689
Instead, for example, the database

35
00:01:35,785 --> 00:01:38,131
connection could fail, so some other

36
00:01:38,212 --> 00:01:40,392
server-side error could occur.

37
00:01:42,004 --> 00:01:44,268
And to simulate this, I'll add an if check

38
00:01:44,268 --> 00:01:46,335
here after this validation error.

39
00:01:47,139 --> 00:01:50,158
And I'll calculate a random number there

40
00:01:50,288 --> 00:01:51,095
with Math.random.

41
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:55,484
And if the number which I derive here is

42
00:01:55,693 --> 00:01:57,589
greater than 0.5,

43
00:01:58,585 --> 00:02:02,410
it will be between 0 and 1. So in 50% of all

44
00:02:02,410 --> 00:02:04,222
cases, we'll make it into this if block.

45
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:06,796
If that's the case, I wanna return a

46
00:02:06,796 --> 00:02:09,774
response that actually outputs some

47
00:02:10,065 --> 00:02:11,878
server-side error message.

48
00:02:13,556 --> 00:02:15,842
And I'll simulate that here simply by then

49
00:02:16,035 --> 00:02:17,275
outputting a paragraph

50
00:02:18,047 --> 00:02:20,317
with a class of error, let's say, where I

51
00:02:20,397 --> 00:02:24,077
say a server-side error occurred,

52
00:02:24,739 --> 00:02:27,048
please try again, something like that.

53
00:02:28,914 --> 00:02:31,740
Again, this is just a demo. In a real app,

54
00:02:31,966 --> 00:02:34,469
that could be a failing database connection

55
00:02:34,469 --> 00:02:35,519
or something like that.

56
00:02:37,287 --> 00:02:39,721
Now, the problem we'll have here

57
00:02:40,256 --> 00:02:41,638
is that if I save that

58
00:02:42,763 --> 00:02:45,301
and I reload and enter some valid

59
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:46,153
credentials here,

60
00:02:47,406 --> 00:02:48,595
you see sometimes

61
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:50,879
this error might occur, not always, but

62
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:53,309
sometimes in 50% of all cases.

63
00:02:55,032 --> 00:02:56,541
And of course, outputting the error message

64
00:02:56,638 --> 00:02:58,407
like this is not bad,

65
00:02:58,991 --> 00:03:01,571
but we might wanna output it in a different

66
00:03:01,587 --> 00:03:01,798
way.

67
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:05,963
We might wanna output it here after the

68
00:03:05,963 --> 00:03:08,816
image, before our inputs, for example.

69
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:13,494
And that would then be a problem because the

70
00:03:13,494 --> 00:03:14,041
target

71
00:03:14,604 --> 00:03:15,664
of this form element,

72
00:03:16,725 --> 00:03:19,199
so for this POST request and the response of

73
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,131
this POST request,

74
00:03:21,352 --> 00:03:23,280
is this extra information div.

75
00:03:24,341 --> 00:03:27,189
And that should be the target for validation

76
00:03:27,237 --> 00:03:31,399
errors, but not for server-side errors as

77
00:03:31,626 --> 00:03:32,872
I'm simulating it here.

78
00:03:35,291 --> 00:03:38,456
And that's where the Retarget header can

79
00:03:38,488 --> 00:03:41,927
help because that header allows me to change

80
00:03:41,959 --> 00:03:45,429
the target for a specific response. So to

81
00:03:45,799 --> 00:03:48,370
override the setting I defined with

82
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:50,121
HX-Target on the client.

83
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:53,254
And that's exactly what I wanna do here for

84
00:03:53,302 --> 00:03:54,893
this server-side error.

85
00:03:56,002 --> 00:03:59,022
If we have such an error, I'll add this

86
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:03,784
hx-retarget header here and I'll change the

87
00:04:03,784 --> 00:04:04,244
target.

88
00:04:06,092 --> 00:04:09,941
And here I'll change it to the first div

89
00:04:10,281 --> 00:04:11,704
with a class of control.

90
00:04:13,289 --> 00:04:15,375
And I then also wanna change the swapping

91
00:04:15,375 --> 00:04:18,208
strategy and make sure that I insert the

92
00:04:18,208 --> 00:04:21,155
response content in front of this element,

93
00:04:21,429 --> 00:04:24,617
not inside of it, not instead of it, but in

94
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:25,406
front of it.

95
00:04:27,459 --> 00:04:29,089
And I'll show you how to do that in a

96
00:04:29,089 --> 00:04:32,010
second. First, let's select this and I'll

97
00:04:32,010 --> 00:04:33,639
select it by that class here.

98
00:04:35,098 --> 00:04:38,231
So I'll set this array target header here to

99
00:04:40,063 --> 00:04:42,554
.control and that will select the first

100
00:04:42,554 --> 00:04:45,756
element with a CSS class of control on that

101
00:04:45,836 --> 00:04:46,143
page.

102
00:04:47,771 --> 00:04:49,721
Now I'll temporarily change this to greater

103
00:04:49,721 --> 00:04:52,349
than 0 so that this will always occur.

104
00:04:53,181 --> 00:04:55,722
Just so that I can show you how this will

105
00:04:55,786 --> 00:04:58,230
work without having to retry it multiple

106
00:04:58,230 --> 00:04:58,586
times.

107
00:04:59,772 --> 00:05:01,436
And therefore now if we save that and reload

108
00:05:02,518 --> 00:05:04,796
and I enter some valid credentials, now you

109
00:05:04,796 --> 00:05:07,429
see it's inserted here instead of that first

110
00:05:07,526 --> 00:05:10,096
input element or this first control div.

111
00:05:12,238 --> 00:05:14,086
That's not what I want though. Instead, I

112
00:05:14,183 --> 00:05:17,020
want to change the swapping strategy and

113
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:20,233
therefore we also need the hx-reswap header,

114
00:05:21,277 --> 00:05:23,621
which allows us to change the swapping

115
00:05:23,621 --> 00:05:26,784
strategy and override the setting that was

116
00:05:26,816 --> 00:05:29,674
defined with hx-swap on the frontend.

117
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:33,624
And we can use the same values as we can for

118
00:05:33,624 --> 00:05:36,498
hx-swap. And therefore, if I wanna insert

119
00:05:36,595 --> 00:05:38,778
the response content in front of the

120
00:05:38,778 --> 00:05:42,744
selected element, I need the before-begin

121
00:05:42,889 --> 00:05:43,917
strategy here.

122
00:05:45,509 --> 00:05:49,526
Therefore, I'll also add this hx-reswap

123
00:05:49,526 --> 00:05:50,048
header here.

124
00:05:52,010 --> 00:05:52,207
And

125
00:05:52,767 --> 00:05:55,797
here it's before begin. That's my strategy.

126
00:05:58,262 --> 00:05:59,981
With that, if we save this,

127
00:06:00,817 --> 00:06:01,363
reload,

128
00:06:03,565 --> 00:06:05,718
enter some valid credentials and click

129
00:06:05,718 --> 00:06:08,546
login, now you see the error message is

130
00:06:08,729 --> 00:06:09,527
inserted here.

131
00:06:12,258 --> 00:06:14,107
And that's therefore another pretty

132
00:06:14,107 --> 00:06:16,406
convenient feature because sometimes you

133
00:06:16,422 --> 00:06:18,833
have a situation like this where you might

134
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:21,309
need different targets and strategies for

135
00:06:21,406 --> 00:06:23,801
different responses. And by setting those

136
00:06:23,897 --> 00:06:26,534
headers, you have that fine-grained control.
